  "security_implications": "The subtraction that generates num_rounds_regular wraps on a zero input, potentially causing an incorrect AES round count. This can break encryption/decryption integrity, leak information, or allow a security bypass. The module also interfaces with key clear, data clear, error, and alert signals; mishandling of round count could propagate into these security-critical outputs. The parameter SecMasking controls whether the PRNG reseed input is used; when masking is disabled, prng_reseed_i is tied off, which may affect reseeding behavior in non-masked configurations.",
